# System dependencies (install before using this project)
# Linux (Ubuntu/Debian): sudo apt-get install <package>
# macOS (Homebrew): brew install <package>  — skip bubblewrap (Mac uses Seatbelt natively)
python3>=3.12
python3-pip
git
bubblewrap  # Linux only; macOS uses Apple Seatbelt (sandbox-exec) — built in
# poppler-utils: pdftotext + pdftoppm. NOT optional — these paths depend on it:
#   (1) Stage 5 build-verify check 5 greps the rendered PDF for residual PLACEHOLDER
#       tokens; with pdftotext absent the pipe feeds grep empty input and the gate
#       silently returns 0 (false PASS on a paper whose title page says TITLE PLACEHOLDER).
#   (2) arpipeline.sty's Layer-4 fingerprint readback (pdftotext paper.pdf | grep ARPIPELINE-FP-V1).
#   (3) --mode report on a PDF-only submission: every audit agent reads submission/paper.pdf.
#       pdftotext extracts its prose; pdftoppm rasterizes pages for agents reading it
#       visually. Without them the fan-out halts rather than "auditing" an unread file.
#   (4) Figure producers (empiricist, theory-explorer, experiment-designer) rasterize
#       PDF-only figures to .png via pdftoppm so paper-writer (no Bash) can see them.
poppler-utils  # macOS Homebrew: brew install poppler
# Python package manager: curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
uv
